WEBVTT

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:28.800
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:28.800
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:28.800
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:53.100 --> 00:02:02.350
Chapter V

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:10.600
On December 4th of Space
Year 745, Imperial Year 436...

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:16.790
...each of humanity's two major military forces
deployed enormous fleets in the Tiamat Starzone.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:18.520
<b>Alliance Fleet Flagship - Hard-luck</b>

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:24.650
The Alliance Fleet's command
staff in this battle was as follows:

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:28.370
Space Fleet Chief Commander -
 Admiral Bruce Ashbey

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:32.240
Space Fleet Chief of Staff -
Vice Admiral Alfred Rosas.

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:35.650
4th Fleet Commander -
Vice Admiral Frederick Jasper.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.400
5th Fleet Commander -
 Vice Admiral Wallice Warwick

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:43.050
8th Fleet Commander -
Vice Admiral Fang Tchew-ling.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:47.490
9th Fleet Commander -
Vice Admiral Vittorio di Bertini.

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:52.300
11th Fleet Commander -
Vice Admiral John Drinker Cope.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:03:00.000
Six fleets, totaling 48,000 ships and 3,636,000
crewmen, were mobilized for this battle.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.230
This was the largest deployment of 
Alliance Fleet assets in its history to date...

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:07.850
...but such a huge undertaking
could not help but draw criticism.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:10.310
The campaign has been
decided upon, hasn't it ?

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:12.780
Is the core of the group
once again the 730 Mafia ?

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:16.550
Is it true that this will be a larger
battle than that of Dagon Starzone ?

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:18.220
This is not a battle.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:21.610
It's just a private
picnic for the 730 Mafia.

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:25.640
They take lots of soldiers with them and just gloat over their battlefield achievements.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:29.650
Because there's military within our government and there's a private clique within the military...

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:31.810
...I dare say there's even the
possibility of a military government.

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:33.750
Whose ?

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:36.720
I'll win this battle, and
I'll become a Fleet Admiral.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:41.250
But then, there will be no
more ladders for me to climb.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:44.620
I wouldn't want to follow in the
footsteps of Limpao or Tparl.

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:48.550
Admiral, was that a declaration of
your interest in pursuing politics...

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:51.650
...that you wouldn't want to be like the two
Fleet Admirals who did not go into politics...

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:55.350
...and lived quiet lives after their
retirement from the military ?

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:01.050
The Admiral has a tendency to make
intentionally controversial remarks...

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.100
...but is this another
example of that ?

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:05.750
What do you think of
military government ?

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:12.300
The politicians' concerns
might have been unwarranted.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:18.890
The 730 Mafia was not a group formed
by a common desire for more power.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:23.390
There was another reason that the
politicians' worries were for naught;

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:25.600
...shortly before the
2nd Battle of Tiamat...

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:29.570
...there was serious dissension among
the members of the 730 Mafia.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:32.700
There's no need
for more explanation !

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:33.940
Just do what I say !

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:36.380
What do you
mean by that ?

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:39.850
This so-called strategy is nothing
more than theory and supposition !

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:43.200
How can I put my faith in 
something so tenuous and flimsy ?

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:47.500
It sounds like all you want from us is blind,
unthinking obedience ? We're better than that !

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:49.860
What's wrong with you ?!

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:52.720
You are the
one who's wrong.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:54.510
I'm the chief
commander here !

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:58.270
My strategies have worked
perfectly up to today.

00:04:58.270 --> 00:04:59.940
And you followed them
without complaint, too.

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:03.690
I had complaints before, too.

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:06.600
But this time around, the
size of our fleet is much larger.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:09.620
We're not in a situation where we
can put complete faith in a strategy...

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:12.000
...that's based on loose
ground and intuition !

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:15.600
No matter the size of the fleet,
what I do is never wrong !

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:18.550
There's no point in
arguing because I'm right !

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:22.950
All you have to do is follow your orders
without complaint like you've always done !

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:34.950
Okay, I understand.

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:37.890
There's no point in
talking about this anymore.

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:43.290
You've changed, Ashbey.

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:47.130
Or were you always like
this and I was just blind ?

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:54.600
In the past, instances of
quarrels and insults weren't rare.

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:59.300
Rather, such good natured confrontations
invigorated the commanding headquarters...

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:02.990
...and led to the creation of new
tactics that contributed to victory.

00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:05.650
Ashbey was not only
a talented tactician...

00:06:05.650 --> 00:06:08.720
...but also the centerpiece of a
staff blessed with talent and vigor.

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:12.310
But in regards to this battle,
he was strangely authoritarian...

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:15.220
...and was reluctant to give
explanations for his tactical plans.

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:18.490
That was certainly the
cause of this cacophony. {among 730 Mafia}

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:23.390
Vittorio di Bertini was 
melancholic, more than usual.

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:30.290
It was purely personal, but, just prior to
his mobilization, all his tropical fish died.

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:34.050
This was because of his wife's inattention,
and shocked by the occurrence...

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:37.390
...Bertini yelled at her for the
first time in their marriage...

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:40.290
...and departed for this deployment, leaving his wife in tears.

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:44.750
He later regretted it, but by then
he had already left Heinessen...

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:46.840
...so he did not have an
opportunity to make up with her.

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:51.570
Can we defeat the
Imperial fleet like this ?

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:54.900
I've never seen the
admirals in such a state.

00:06:57.420 --> 00:07:02.850
But according to March Jasper's
jinx, this is a turn for victory.

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:07.020
But March Jasper isn't the
only commander in this battle.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:12.100
Even if the 4th Fleet wins its part of the
battle, we could lose the battle as a whole.

00:07:12.550 --> 00:07:14.040
Don't worry too much.

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:17.600
Admiral Ashbey is the chief
commander, so we'll probably be okay.

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:20.120
He's a genius, after all.

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:23.650
Well...what do we do if the enemy
has an even bigger genius ?

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:25.060
"What do we do ?"

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:27.080
Don't ask me.

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:30.390
Just ask the admirals,
"What are the chances of victory ?"

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:32.760
How can I ask something like that ?

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:37.500
They'll just yell, "If you don't have the
will to win at all costs, how can we win ?"

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:42.390
Some people would say that is more
important than supplies and information.

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:46.080
The 730 Mafia isn't a bunch of idiot brass-hats. They're not like that

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:47.260
I sure hope so.

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:55.100
The soldiers couldn't easily grasp
the meaning of fighting and winning.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:08:00.520
Fighting for 100 years against the evil, autocratic empire that Rudolph von Goldenbaum built...

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:07.260
...they'd been told they were protecting peace and justice in the universe.

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:12.460
But they couldn't sustain such high morale forever and keep fighting.

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:15.610
Still, the Alliance might
have been better off...

00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:19.070
...because they at least had the
conviction that it was a protective war.

00:08:19.070 --> 00:08:23.690
Though victory might gain them little, defeat would surely mean the loss of all they held dear.

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:28.050
The Imperial Fleet,
on the other hand...

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:32.670
...was only concerned with what victory might bring them and not with thoughts of loss or defeat.

00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:37.300
The commander was Space Fleet
Chief Commander, Fleet Admiral Zeiten.

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:37.300
<b>Imperial Fleet Flagship - Audhumla</b>

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:39.750
To guarantee his victory, the Fleet
Admiral mobilized an unprecedented fleet...

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:46.630
...totaling 7 fleets - 56,000 ships and 6,500,000 crewmen.

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:45.910
<b>Space Fleet Chief Commander, Fleet Admiral Zeiten</b>

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:49.500
<b>Muckenberger Fleet Flagship - Kurmark</b>

00:08:47.390 --> 00:08:52.300
Recently deceased Chief of the Ministry of
the Military, Fleet Admiral Keltring's nephew...

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:57.400
...Vice Admiral Wilhelm von Muckenberger, led a fleet that had especially high morale.

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:01.200
<b>Vice Admiral Wilhelm von Muckenberger</b>

00:08:58.350 --> 00:08:59.780
Attention, all crews.

00:08:59.780 --> 00:09:01.200
This is a battle of revenge.

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:04.050
By beheading the
rebel leader, Ashbey...

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:06.910
...we will wreak vengeance for the
General of the Military Ministry.

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:11.130
The one who takes Ashbey's head
will be given any reward he wants.

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:13.280
All of you,
we must win !

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:14.530
Yeah !

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:22.800
However, Vice Admiral Hauser von Steiermark was critical of Vice Admiral Muckenberger's speech.

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:20.650
<b>Steiermark Fleet Flagship - Vanadis</b>

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:23.700
<b>Vice Admiral Hauser von Steiermark</b>

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:27.210
That's like promoting
your own private war.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:30.400
If killing just one rebel commander named
Ashbey is the sole purpose of our battle...

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:35.110
...our sense of priorities
will need to be questioned.

00:09:35.110 --> 00:09:37.050
The commanders of
the Imperial Fleet...

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:40.910
...often think of battlefields as
places to garner personal accolades.

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:43.670
Therefore, they tend to be poor at
cooperating with other commanders...

00:09:43.670 --> 00:09:45.960
...and have little feelings
for their soldiers.

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:47.590
That's a concern.

00:09:47.590 --> 00:09:50.730
But we have the
size advantage.

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:55.100
Even though they know the
terrain better, we won't yield.

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:57.360
I hope so.

00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:01.460
Steiermark's concerns
later became reality.

00:10:04.230 --> 00:10:07.050
On December 5th, at 9:50...

00:10:07.050 --> 00:10:11.400
...the two sides within the Tiamat
Starzone finally exchanged fire.

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:23.220
Contact with the enemy
fleet has been confirmed.

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:26.050
Advance !

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:27.830
Thrust through the middle of the enemy's
center and right wing deployments.

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:34.650
<b>11th Fleet Flagship - Vivasvat</b>

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:34.650
Light signal acknowledged !

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:38.700
What should we do, Commander ?

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:40.910
We'll follow orders.

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:41.650
Advance.

00:10:41.670 --> 00:10:43.700
<b>9th Fleet Flagship - Tlahuixcalpantecuhtli</b>

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:49.410
Two fleets from the rebel forces
are quickly advancing toward us.

00:10:50.490 --> 00:10:55.050
Keep an eye on the movement of their main fleet and concentrate fire on the advancing fleets.

00:11:05.530 --> 00:11:06.770
Don't allow them
to come near us !

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:14.900
The enemy is concentrating fire on the
9th Fleet, and they're coming to a halt.

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:18.450
Too bad for Bertini, but
I'll make him be our shield.

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:20.310
This is our chance -
we will advance !

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:27.100
Don't permit a breakthrough !

00:11:27.100 --> 00:11:28.490
Stop their frontline !

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:37.670
The enemy fleet
is blocking our path.

00:11:38.930 --> 00:11:39.950
Damn.

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:41.240
The enemy fleets
have stopped advancing.

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:43.120
Good.

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:47.350
Go in between the enemy fleets 
and seal off their withdrawal route !

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:53.850
Since the 9th Fleet is late,
its support is becoming ineffective.

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:56.300
The 11th Fleet may be
isolated inside enemy territory.

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:12.120
Cope has become a drunkard,
just as his name is.

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:16.410
Pay him a visit, give him
some water and wake him up.

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:19.010
As you wish.

00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:22.460
<b>5th Fleet Flagship - Lugeilan</b>

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:27.670
Jasper, the objective of the enemy
is to attack us from behind...

00:12:27.670 --> 00:12:30.190
...following a large-scale
back turn movement.

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:36.650
Their numbers are almost half their fleet,
estimated to be approximately 23,000 ships.

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:39.840
I want you to stop
this with your fleet.

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:41.310
With only my fleet ?

00:12:41.310 --> 00:12:43.100
The enemy is almost
three times larger.

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:46.750
The enemy will most
likely take this route.

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:52.370
Here, because of the effect of the asteroids and permanent star, they can't deploy their large fleet.

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:55.050
A small fleet can more
than hold its own.

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:58.050
Destroy them, March Jasper.

00:13:00.650 --> 00:13:02.370
I got it.

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:04.330
But is that
information reliable ?

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:06.360
That's something General
Headquarters decides.

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:09.460
On the frontlines, you just have to trust me and follow my orders.

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:14.770
All right, I'll
follow your orders.

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:18.500
But if things don't go the way
you say, I'll do as I like.

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:20.370
That won't happen.

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:21.870
I hope you're right.

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:28.880
Commander, with what little information
we have, how did you figure it out{i.e. the opposition's strategy} ?

00:13:28.880 --> 00:13:30.480
I just know.{can figure it out.}

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:31.600
That's all.

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:32.560
Huh ?

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:40.180
Bruce, aren't you being
a little too dogmatic ?

00:13:40.180 --> 00:13:42.110
Don't worry, Alfred.

00:13:42.110 --> 00:13:43.390
All's well.

00:13:43.390 --> 00:13:45.940
More importantly, what's
the 5th Fleet's status ?

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:47.750
They will contact the
enemy fleet shortly.

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:56.000
We'll attack the left rear of the Imperial
Fleet that is dividing the 9th and 11th Fleets.

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:56.690
Hurry !

00:13:57.460 --> 00:13:59.930
Enemy fleet is approaching
from our port aft.

00:13:59.930 --> 00:14:00.840
They're about to attack !

00:14:01.810 --> 00:14:04.930
At this rate, we could
be semi-encircled.

00:14:04.930 --> 00:14:06.350
Pull yourself together.

00:14:07.030 --> 00:14:13.740
We'll annihilate the fleet in front of us, move past them, join our allies, then attack the enemy behind us.

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:17.050
First, concentrate on destroying the
enemy in front of us and move forward.

00:14:17.050 --> 00:14:17.800
Hurry !

00:14:22.300 --> 00:14:24.390
There's the reinforcements
from our side.

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:26.870
When the enemy fleet gets
pushed forward, attack them !

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:31.190
Commander, the other ships
are not keeping up with us.

00:14:31.190 --> 00:14:33.440
Our ship is getting
too far forward.

00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:34.150
What ?

00:14:34.150 --> 00:14:35.770
An enemy ship is closing
in on us dead ahead !

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:37.460
Turn around !

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:01.160
Uncle, I'm sorry.

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:12.950
Wilhelmina, take good care of Gregor so he
will become a distinguished serviceman...

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:18.500
...and then, Gregor, take
my revenge upon them...

00:15:22.490 --> 00:15:24.940
We've sunk the enemy flagship !
The enemy fleet is in disarray !

00:15:25.390 --> 00:15:26.310
This is a good chance for us !

00:15:26.310 --> 00:15:28.390
Let's break through
immediately and withdraw !

00:15:28.390 --> 00:15:30.390
Concentrate our attack !

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:37.460
We'll aid the withdrawal
of the 11th Fleet.

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:39.280
Increase the distance between ships
and put pressure on the enemy !

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:52.410
Don't get any further
behind that fleet !

00:15:52.410 --> 00:15:54.630
Avoid enemy fire and
attack with all ships !

00:15:54.630 --> 00:15:55.400
Hurry !

00:15:57.760 --> 00:16:01.950
Bertini, the sleeping giant,
has finally woken up.

00:16:01.950 --> 00:16:05.910
No, it's more appropriate to say that the
bear has come out of hibernation, right ?

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:11.520
In the initial stage of the battle, we can safely say that the Alliance held the advantage.

00:16:11.520 --> 00:16:16.180
They sank Vice Admiral Muckenberger's ship, and practically wiped out his fleet.

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:20.460
That proved the brilliance
of each fleet commander...

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:24.080
...but the timing of Ashbey's reinforcement orders had a touch of genius.

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:26.570
The 11th Fleet seems to
have escaped the crisis.

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:32.040
The 11th Fleet has returned
to the battle line.

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:33.080
All right.

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:34.730
We'll follow it up
with a victory.

00:16:34.730 --> 00:16:37.720
Quickly move forward and push aside
the Imperial Fleet to the left front.

00:16:38.710 --> 00:16:43.000
Form an arc, attack one side of the enemy
fleet and break up their fleet formation.

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:45.740
Commander, we must ask for
Headquarters' permission.

00:16:45.740 --> 00:16:47.270
I don't care !

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:50.550
I'm tired of letting Bruce
monopolize all the credit.

00:16:50.550 --> 00:16:55.400
We deserve at least one rose
from all those bouquets.

00:16:56.060 --> 00:16:57.110
Commander...

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:00.510
I understand.

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:04.610
The 5th Fleet is
moving forward !

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:06.180
What ?

00:17:07.330 --> 00:17:08.190
Commander...

00:17:08.600 --> 00:17:10.230
His thinking is right on.

00:17:10.230 --> 00:17:12.230
But will the enemy sit still ?

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:15.520
In accordance with Ashbey's
prediction, or rather misgivings...

00:17:15.520 --> 00:17:20.990
...the Imperial Steiermark Fleet started moving
in reaction to the movement of the 5th Fleet.

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:25.420
And their movements were
swifter than that of the 5th Fleet.

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:30.020
When the 5th Fleet quickly moved toward
the 2 o'clock direction forming an arc...

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:34.650
...the Steiermark Fleet launched an
attack from the 8 o'clock direction...

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:36.870
...using a similar
circular movement.

00:17:37.390 --> 00:17:42.420
As a result, the Alliance Fleet essentially helped the Imperial Fleet succeed in its left flank-rear attack.

00:17:44.550 --> 00:17:45.500
Dammit !

00:17:54.100 --> 00:17:57.650
B...B...B-04 cannon,
B-04 cannon, respond !

00:17:57.960 --> 00:17:59.160
B-04 cannon !

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:04.440
This is B-04 cannon, operator
Sergeant Alexander Bucock.

00:18:04.440 --> 00:18:06.160
B-04 cannon, why
aren't you firing ?

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:08.500
I have no ammunition left.

00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:09.100
What ?

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:11.520
I used it all up in
the previous battle.

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:24.600
In the next battle, I'll have to use
ammunition more effectively.

00:18:29.100 --> 00:18:32.300
That is, if there is such
a thing as the "next battle."

00:18:38.740 --> 00:18:40.950
The enemy fleet has broken through our center section.

00:18:40.950 --> 00:18:41.900
They're penetrating
our lines even further.

00:18:42.610 --> 00:18:44.180
Damn.  There's no
other way out.

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:45.460
Open communications with
General Headquarters.

00:18:47.650 --> 00:18:49.310
There's a message
from the 5th Fleet.

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:51.960
"I have been impaled through
the back to chest..."

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:55.070
"...and my wound is getting larger
as the spear is being turned."

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:55.810
That's all.

00:18:56.410 --> 00:18:59.070
That's an expression
appropriate for Warwick.

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:00.760
Is he asking for
reinforcements ?

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:02.650
It doesn't definitively say.

00:19:02.650 --> 00:19:03.990
That image-conscious bastard.

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:05.770
He can't even ask for
help straightforwardly.

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:06.550
What should we do ?

00:19:10.350 --> 00:19:10.900
Commander ?

00:19:11.320 --> 00:19:12.240
Commander ?

00:19:12.240 --> 00:19:14.380
Well, leave him
alone for a while.

00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:16.880
Bruce, what the...?

00:19:17.600 --> 00:19:20.240
I won't abandon him,
so don't worry.

00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:22.020
But I have an idea.

00:19:22.020 --> 00:19:22.720
Just watch.

00:19:25.030 --> 00:19:26.240
What's happening with
General Headquarters ?

00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:28.220
They haven't said a word.

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:32.140
Bruce, is he going to make an example out of me for my arbitrary decision and execution ?

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:33.750
Commander...

00:19:33.750 --> 00:19:37.490
At this stage, we'll have to do something about it ourselves, or else I'll lose face.

00:19:37.490 --> 00:19:38.570
Let's shift our viewpoint.

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:40.870
Don't think of it as allowing
a center-section breakthrough.

00:19:40.870 --> 00:19:42.880
Think of it as a chance
for an enveloping attack.

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:53.960
This is...

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:56.110
Is something wrong ?

00:19:56.110 --> 00:20:01.760
I know that the enemy's 9th and 11th Fleets can't move, since they're engaged with our main fleet.

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:06.930
But why aren't they sending reinforcements
to the 5th Fleet that we broke through ?

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:08.460
What do you think,
Chief Staff Officer ?

00:20:08.460 --> 00:20:12.220
It certainly seems that their
main fleet is holding back.

00:20:12.220 --> 00:20:15.400
Display the plot of the
enemy's positions and movements.

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:16.210
Yes, sir !

00:20:19.950 --> 00:20:21.030
Just as I thought.

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:23.740
The enemy has figured
out our back-turn advancement.

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:27.400
Not only that, I can't help but think that
they're holding back their main fleet...

00:20:27.400 --> 00:20:29.600
...so they can launch a
rear flanking attack on us.

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:32.240
It's dangerous to continue
with our tactical plan.

00:20:32.240 --> 00:20:34.300
We must report this to
General Headquarters immediately.

00:20:34.850 --> 00:20:36.270
But we're in the
middle of the battle.

00:20:36.270 --> 00:20:37.350
I know that.

00:20:37.350 --> 00:20:38.670
Prepare to launch a
communication shuttle.

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:39.730
I'll have it
deliver the report.

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:50.290
The communication shuttle
seems to have been lost.

00:20:50.290 --> 00:20:51.330
What ?

00:20:53.700 --> 00:20:55.250
Should we send
a second shuttle ?

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:58.070
Or should we use radio communications
and risk getting intercepted ?

00:20:58.640 --> 00:21:00.280
No, we don't have
any time left.

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:02.360
We'll join the main fleet.

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:06.860
But, Commander, it's very difficult
to withdraw our ships at this stage.

00:21:06.860 --> 00:21:09.200
The enemy won't let us
withdraw easily, either.

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:10.500
I know.

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:13.750
But fortunately, we're right inside
the center section of the enemy fleet.

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:15.430
We'll keep this direction
and break through.

00:21:15.430 --> 00:21:18.110
Then we'll join the left
wing of the main fleet.

00:21:18.110 --> 00:21:20.050
As soon as we
secure this space area...

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:23.090
...I will go directly to Headquarters
to explain the situation.

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:24.840
That'll probably work better.

00:21:27.290 --> 00:21:29.960
The enemy fleet is
separating from us.

00:21:29.960 --> 00:21:33.160
It looks like we've allowed a
center-section breakthrough, but...

00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:34.000
Damn.

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:38.350
I hate looking bad but it's better
than having them stay in the middle.

00:21:38.350 --> 00:21:39.750
Hurry up and regroup.

00:21:39.750 --> 00:21:44.150
We'll withdraw to the 9th and 11th Fleets' line
for the time being and redo our formation.

00:21:44.150 --> 00:21:45.010
Yes, sir.

00:21:45.010 --> 00:21:49.870
In any case, did Ashbey not mobilize his fleet
because he knew this was going to happen ?

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:51.900
Even though he knew I
was fighting a tough battle.

00:21:54.560 --> 00:21:56.650
Just as I thought, the
enemy fleet withdrew first.

00:21:57.550 --> 00:21:59.690
You knew this, too ?

00:21:59.690 --> 00:22:01.800
No, I made it that way.

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:05.370
The Imperial fleet will suspend their
initial plan of a back-turn advancement...

00:22:05.370 --> 00:22:08.350
...followed by attacks from both
sides and they will try to regroup.

00:22:08.350 --> 00:22:11.180
We'll call back Jasper
and regroup, too.

00:22:11.910 --> 00:22:16.940
In the first half of the battle, we could say that Ashbey's god-given talents were in full force.

00:22:17.360 --> 00:22:21.350
The 5th Fleet has regrouped,
and is returning to the fleet line.

00:22:21.350 --> 00:22:24.930
We'll withdraw all fleets 5 light seconds
for the time being and regroup.

00:22:24.930 --> 00:22:26.670
Let's do it - the battle has only begun !

00:22:28.110 --> 00:22:31.050
How did he take hold of
such chances for victory ?

00:22:31.050 --> 00:22:33.930
Is it because of supernatural power
that could only be explained...

00:22:33.930 --> 00:22:38.560
...as being loved by the Goddess
of Victory, or Goddess of Time ?

00:22:38.560 --> 00:22:39.480
Or...

00:22:40.990 --> 00:22:45.520
But it may be too hasty to ask for an
answer to that question just now.

00:22:45.520 --> 00:22:48.450
The 2nd Battle of
Tiamat had only begun...

00:22:48.450 --> 00:22:51.550
...and even with the annihilation
of the Muckenberger Fleet...

00:22:51.550 --> 00:22:54.980
...the Imperial Fleet still held the size advantage.

00:22:54.980 --> 00:23:01.300
Whether or not Ashbey was indeed loved by the Goddess of Time would eventually be tested.

00:22:59.370 --> 00:23:04.300
The Man Whom the Goddess of Time Loved

00:22:59.370 --> 00:23:04.300
-The Chronicle of the 2nd Battle of Tiamat, Part I-

